<title>BELGIUM: EU likely to probe Krupp bid for Thyssen.</title>
<headline>EU likely to probe Krupp bid for Thyssen.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission had no comment on Tuesday on Krupp's planned takeover of rival Thyssen AG, but EU sources said that the case would probably have to be examined under EU competition rules.</p>
<p>&quot;We have not received anything either from the Bundeskartellamt or the companies involved,&quot; the spokesman for European Competition Commissioner Karel Van Miert told reporters.</p>
<p>But the other sources thought the Commission would almost certainly have the power to investigate the bid because of the companies' significant sales outside Germany.</p>
<p>Under the European Union's merger rules, a deal may be examined by national competition authorities, rather than the Commission, if the companies involved do more than two thirds of their turnover in one and same country.</p>
<p>-- Brussels newsroom 322 2876841</p>
</text>
